{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":156820,"duration_api_ms":156724,"num_turns":7,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"cd2d096b-dff7-403c-a4aa-e622dd5e5e48","total_cost_usd":0.5457546999999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":38076,"cache_read_input_tokens":180525,"output_tokens":4131,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":38076,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":6,"outputTokens":4131,"cacheReadInputTokens":180525,"cacheCreationInputTokens":38076,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.43154249999999994,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000},"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":29,"outputTokens":12640,"cacheReadInputTokens":92232,"cacheCreationInputTokens":33408,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.11421220000000001,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"summary":"Evaluated 5 amendments against the current codebase. Three are valid low-risk improvements (naming convention discovery, clarifying comment, test robustness). One identifies a genuine biological modeling error in plant/algae respiration routing. One amendment (shrimp water-column fallback) describes behavior that does not exist in the current code and must be rejected.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-8-37900497","decision":"accept","rationale":"Valid maintainability concern. is_shared_budget_path hard-codes 'animal.adults_count' and 'animal.juveniles_count' in a matches! arm, meaning any future count-based mass pool (e.g. larvae_count) would be silently missed by the structural coverage test. Adding a doc comment on AnimalState flagging which count fields carry implicit mass, or adding a convention-based suffix check, is low-risk and prevents a real class of future bug."},{"amendment_id":"fr-8-1415e3ec","decision":"accept","rationale":"The amendment correctly identifies that dissolved_feed_residue_g_total is reduced by the water change retention factor (line 60) but this reduction is not reflected in the budget export delta. As stated, this has zero impact on mass conservation since the residue counter mirrors DOC/DON already tracked. Adding a clarifying comment at that line is essentially free and prevents a future developer from mistakenly adding it to the budget delta (which would cause double-counting)."},{"amendment_id":"fr-8-2fe7314b","decision":"accept","rationale":"The tests sum particulate_organics_g_total + fine_detritus_g_total before conversion, which masks the individual component conversions due to linearity. While the production code currently uses the same detritus_nitrogen_mg/detritus_carbon_mg for both, splitting the computation in the test would independently verify each component's conversion. This is a trivial change that improves test sensitivity to potential future divergence in detritus conversion formulas."},{"amendment_id":"fr-8-8959bb9b","decision":"accept","rationale":"Genuine biological modeling error. In plant_growth.rs, route_plant_loss_to_dissolved_organics routes respiration losses directly to DON/DOC (line 157), when respiration should consume O2 and produce DIC/CO2. Similarly in algae_growth.rs, respiration+grazing losses are lumped together and routed to DON/DOC (lines 122, 207-208). The default rates for respiration_dic_rate and photosynthesis_dic_rate are both 0.0 (process.rs:227-228), confirming the DIC/O2 pathway is inactive. Note that plant senescence is correctly routed to fine_detritus (line 158-159), so only the respiration path needs rework. For algae, respiration and grazing losses should be separated — respiration to DIC/O2, grazing waste to detritus or dissolved organics. The budget closes but the pathways are biologically wrong."},{"amendment_id":"fr-8-65a8127d","decision":"reject","rationale":"The amendment claims fund_live_shrimp_biomass falls back from animal.reserve_g to dissolved_organic_nitrogen, ammonia_total, dissolved_organic_carbon, and dissolved_inorganic_carbon. This is factually incorrect. The current code at shrimp.rs:636-648 clearly shows fund_live_shrimp_biomass only checks animal.reserve_g and returns false if insufficient — there is no water-column fallback path. Development already fails when reserve is insufficient. The described issue does not exist in the current codebase."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"dd7da1e2-c957-4acd-816c-6a6d348493ae"}
